  "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=3,$ the vector ${r}^{\u2032}(3)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(3)+u{r}^{\u2032}(3),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\u27e8{3}^{3},{3}^{2}-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e827,7\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{t}^{2},2t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ at $t=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(3) & =\u27e83(3)^{2},2(3)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e827,6\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=3$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=\u27e827,7\u27e9+u\u27e827,6\u27e9,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
